        "date": "2026-11-22T07:22:44Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): add the G-EDM 2-axis wire EDM post (g-edm.cps)\n\n\"G-EDM Wire EDM\" is a new wire EDM post for G-EDM builds on G-RBLv3.\nIt writes Grbl-family words only (G21/G20 G90 G17, G0, G1, G2/G3 with\nI J, M30), with no % fence, no O word, no F word and no edm.codes. The\nspark power is set at the controller; the condition id is a comment.\n\nIt writes one vertical 2-axis wire section per program. It refuses by\nname: a non-wire_edm machine, a rotary, edm.awt, taper, 4-axis, U/V,\nangle words, every COMP record, skims, an offset other than G54, a\nspindle, a tool change, a cycle, a Z change, and every stop or home ask.\n\n\"Generic ISO Wire EDM\" stays the default wire post.\n\nFixes #2700\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
